course: dictionary
lesson: 14051
title: A word from the kitchen: marinade
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A marinade is a mix of liquids, herbs and spices that food soaks in before it is cooked. Oil, vinegar, lemon juice and soy sauce are common ingredients. The food soaks up the flavour, and it can get a little softer too.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Mum mixed oil, lemon juice and garlic, then put the chicken in the marinade for an hour.» Oil, lemon, garlic and soaking for an hour tell you that a marinade is a tasty mixture, not a kind of meat or a pudding.
explain: Marinade can also be a verb, mostly in UK English. To marinade or marinate food means to soak it in a marinade. «Leave the tofu to marinade overnight» means soak it overnight. Both verb forms mean the same thing.
fact: A marinade is a mixture of liquids, herbs and spices.
fact: Meat, fish, tofu and vegetables are often soaked in a marinade before cooking.
fact: Acids such as lemon juice, vinegar and yogurt can soften meat a little.
fact: Raw meat marinade must be kept in the fridge, and it must never be used as a sauce unless it has been boiled.
fact: «Marinate» is another verb with the same meaning as «marinade» as a verb.
exercise: «Sam mixed oil, lemon juice and herbs to make a marinade.» What is a marinade? | *A mixture of liquids and flavours that food soaks in before cooking | Cold dessert made with cream | A kind of plate | A tool for cutting meat
exercise: «Leave the chicken in the marinade in the fridge for two hours.» Where should the raw chicken and its marinade be kept? | In the bread bin | In a warm, sunny window | On the kitchen table | *In the fridge
exercise: «Please marinade the tofu for an hour.» What does marinade mean here? | To cut food into small pieces | To burn food on a hot grill | *To soak food in a flavoured mixture | To freeze food solid
test: «Mia marinaded the vegetables overnight.» What does marinaded mean here? | Boiled dry | Frozen solid | *Soaked in a flavoured mixture | Sliced very thin
test: Which ingredient is an acid that can soften meat a little? | Paper | *Lemon juice | Sugar | Flour
exam: Why must raw meat marinade not be used as a sauce unless it is boiled? | Because it tastes better cold | Because it must be frozen before it is eaten | Because it turns into bread | *Raw meat can make it unsafe, so it must be boiled first
